# Convex deployment URL (public, safe to expose in the client bundle).
# Local dev: set by `npx convex dev` (anonymous local deployment).
# On Vercel it is injected automatically by the build command
# (`npx convex deploy --cmd-url-env-var-name PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL ...`).
# Leave empty until the Convex project exists: the contact form
# degrades gracefully and shows a LinkedIn fallback instead.
PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=

# --- Vercel-only variables (never needed locally) -------------------------
# CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY        deploy key of the target Convex deployment
#                          (Production env -> prod key, Preview env -> dev key)
# PUBLIC_SITE_URL          set once the custom domain exists (https://...)
# KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID     \
# KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET  > created by the Keystatic GitHub App
# KEYSTATIC_SECRET                > setup wizard at /keystatic
# PUBLIC_KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_APP_SLUG /
# Locally, Keystatic runs in "local" storage mode and needs none of these.
